# Essence Channeler: paying life is losing life (CR 119.4, 119.3), so once Bot1 pays 1 life for Marsh Flats in its own turn the
# Channeler has flying and vigilance. It attacks beside Bot1's Llanowar Elves: vigilance leaves it untapped (CR 702.20b) while the
# Elves tap, and flying keeps Bot2's Llanowar Elves from blocking it (CR 702.9b, refused) though they can block Bot1's Elves (the
# control). Bot2 takes 2 from the Channeler; the Elves trade.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Plains
Essence Channeler
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Marsh Flats
Plains
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Island x5
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Essence Channeler.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Hand.Marsh Flats.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Marsh Flats.Activate
Bot1.Search(Swamp)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Life = 19
? Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler.Keywords = Flying; Vigilance
Bot1.Attack(Essence Channeler; Llanowar Elves)
! Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Essence Channeler)
Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler.Keywords = Flying; Vigilance
Bot1.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Marsh Flats
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
